## What the content licence covers

Everything under `content/`, and the prose it compiles into: annotations, middlegame plans,
positional assessments, soundness judgements and explanatory text — in Vietnamese, English and
French.

Reusing any of it means **crediting the source** and **sharing your version under the same
licence**. This is deliberate: the annotations are the most expensive part of this project to
produce, and they are the part worth protecting.

## What it does not cover, because it cannot

**Chess moves are not copyrightable.** Moves, positions, games and opening sequences are facts and
game mechanics rather than authorship, and copyright does not protect procedures or processes. The
move sequences in this repository are free for anyone to use, licence or no licence. The licence
applies to the writing about them.

